Braindead 4ever – third-party data

Braindead 4ever's code is licensed under GPL-3.0-or-later with the additional permission in
LICENSE-EXCEPTION.md. The route data is a separate part with its own terms, because it
contains data from the projects below:

  data/sources/polestar/   Polestar forever-db           GPL-3.0-only
  data/sources/eglink/     EG Link output, WoW: Forever  CC BY 4.0
  data/sources/att/        All The Things                MIT
  data/facts/, data/routes/, Braindead4Ever/Routes/Data_*.lua  merged from all three: GPL-3.0-only

These data files do not carry the Ace3 permission of LICENSE-EXCEPTION.md: it can only be
granted by the copyright holders, and the Polestar data is not ours. Data from these projects
starts with the status "unbestätigt" (unconfirmed) and is replaced as soon as our own in-game
measurements cover it. The source form of the compiled data (Braindead4Ever/Routes/Data_*.lua) is
the route files in data/routes and the tools in tools/routekit, published at
https://github.com/chkie/braindead-4ever.

Which version of each source was used is recorded in data/sources/<source>/SOURCE.json and in
the #sources line of every route file.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Polestar forever-db
https://github.com/fitzforge/polestar/tree/next/forever-db

The database tables used (quest, quest_start, quest_end, quest_prereq, quest_objective, npc,
spawn, item_source, ui_map) are licensed under the GNU General Public License version 3 only
(datapackage.json). Polestar's own credits, which also apply to the values taken from it:

- EG Link output: World of Warcraft: Forever (https://github.com/JIVESCORP/eg-link-output-wowf),
  data from Efficient Games (https://efficient.games), licensed under CC BY 4.0.
- CMaNGOS classic-db (https://github.com/cmangos/classic-db), GPL-3.0.
- VMaNGOS values (through pfQuest) and Factoruide data (https://github.com/Factoruide),
  GPL-2.0-or-later.
- ForeverTDB, the Forever TrinityCore world database
  (https://github.com/advocaite/TrinityCore/tree/forever), GPL-2.0.
- QuestieDB (Questie team), credited per its maintainer.
- World of Warcraft: Forever client tables.
- pfQuest (https://github.com/shagu/pfQuest), MIT License, Copyright (c) 2017-2021 Eric Mauser
  (Shagu).

Changed: reduced to quests up to level 34, without titles and names; spawn points reduced to
giver, turn-in and objective positions; NPCs reduced to class trainers, innkeepers and flight
masters with role, class, faction template, a side derived from it and their spawn points,
without titles and names.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
EG Link output: World of Warcraft: Forever
https://github.com/JIVESCORP/eg-link-output-wowf

Data from Efficient Games (https://efficient.games), licensed under CC BY 4.0
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).

Changed: reduced to quest facts (who offers and takes a quest and where players stood, which
faction the server describes a quest for, quest level, minimum level and race mask), to the
start positions of new characters, to class trainers, innkeepers and flight masters (the window
a player opened, side, flight point, where players stood) and to flights (the flight points of
each trip, how many flights took how many seconds); merged over the builds of the products
wow_classic_beta and wowf; coordinates reordered to north and west. No game text is included.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
All The Things (Forever database)
https://github.com/ATTWoWAddon/AllTheThings/tree/master/.contrib/.db/forever

Changed: quest facts only (quest IDs, giver IDs, coordinates, prerequisites, races, classes,
required level, flags) and the discovery catalog (treasures, books, rares, flight points with the
NPC ID of their flight master), read from the Lua source files; no names or comments.

